端到端的 MLOPS、生命周期以及 MLOPS 的职业机会。
and model drip, end-to-end MLOPs, lifecycle and career opportunities in MLOPS.

18
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,760
那么让我们开始吧。
So let's begin.

19
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:32,320
什么是 MLOPS？
What is MLOPS?

20
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:36,160
MLOPS 代表机器学习加上运维。
MLOPS stands for machine learning plus operations.

21
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:46,960
它是工程实践、自动化、基础设施和流程的结合，用于管理机器学习系统从开发到生产的全过程。
It is a combination of engineering practices, automation, infrastructure and
processes used to manage machine learning system from development to production.

22
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:51,600
简单来说，机器学习侧重于创建模型。
Simple meaning, machine learning focuses on creating models.

23
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:59,360
MLOPS 侧重于让这些模型在真实环境中变得可用、可扩展、可靠且可维护。
MLOPS focuses on making those models usable, scalable, reliable and maintainable in real-world environment.

24
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:05,120
你可以这样理解：构建模型就像设计汽车发动机。
You can think of it like this Building a model is like designing a car engine.

25
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:09,348
MLOPS 就是围绕它构建整个运输系统。
MLOPS is building the entire transport system around it.

26
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:15,840
包括燃料系统、道路支持、维护、监控、安全检查、维修流程和升级。
Fuel system, road support, maintenance, monitoring, safety checks, repair process, upgrades.

27
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:20,000
如果没有那个系统，即使是最好的发动机也不够用。
Without that system, even the best engine is not enough.

28
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:26,160
同样，如果没有 MLOPS，即使是高准确率的模型也可能永远无法创造商业价值。
Similarly, without MLOPs, even a high accuracy model may never create business value.

29
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:29,280
为什么单靠机器学习就不够了？
Why machine learning alone is not enough?

30
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:34,436
很多初学者认为，训练模型、保存模型，你的工作就完成了。
Many beginners believe train model, save model and your job is done.

31
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:37,680
但让我们看看在公司里会发生什么。
But let's see what happens in a company.

32
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:41,760
假设你构建了一个客户流失预测模型。
Suppose you build a customer churn prediction model.

33
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:45,680
它能预测哪些客户可能会在下个月流失。
It predicts which customer may leave next month.

34
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,760
模型准确率是 92%，看起来非常出色。
Model accuracy is 92%, looks excellent.

35
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,880
但接着业务团队就问，销售团队能在 CRM 系统里用它吗？
But then business team asks, can sales team use it in CRM system?

36
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,040
预测结果能每天更新吗？
Can prediction refresh every day?

37
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,840
我们能解释为什么客户可能会流失吗？
Can we explain why customer may leave?

38
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,480
如果错误的预测增加了怎么办？
What if wrong prediction increases?

39
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,240
如果服务器崩溃了怎么办？
What if server crashes?

40
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:07,520
如果没有客户行为数据出现怎么办？
What if no customer behavior appears?

41
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:21,252
现在突然发现，单靠机器学习是不够的，因为成功取决于工程系统、部署流程、监控流水线、
基础设施可靠性、数据新鲜度以及团队协作。
Now suddenly machine learning alone is not enough because success depends on engineering system, deployment process,
monitoring pipelines, infrastructure reliability, data freshness, team collaboration.

42
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:25,120
这就是 MLOps 存在的意义。
That is exactly why MROS exist.

43
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:32,720
让我们来看一个银行欺诈检测的真实案例。
Consider one real life example of banking fraud detection.

44
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:36,160
让我们拿一个最典型的现实案例来说。
Let's take one of the best real world examples.

45
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:40,160
银行每天处理数百万笔交易。
Banks process millions of transactions daily.

46
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:43,440
每笔交易都必须在毫秒内完成检查。
Every transaction must be checked in milliseconds.

47
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:50,960
例如刷信用卡、UPI 支付、国际转账、ATM 取款、在线购物等。
For example, credit card swipe, UPI payment, international transfer, ATM withdrawal, online purchases.

48
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:56,160
欺诈检测模型会预测交易是否可疑。
A fraud detection model predicts whether transaction is suspicious.

49
00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:08,560
它可能会分析交易金额、用户位置、时间、设备指纹、消费模式、商户类型以及近期交易频率。
It may analyze transaction amount, user location, time of day, device
fingerprint, spending pattern, merchant type, frequency of recent transactions.

50
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:12,720
现在想象一下，这个模型是八个月前训练的。
Now imagine this model was trained eight months ago.

51
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:16,800
从那时起，诈骗者学会了新技术。
Since then, fraudsters learn new techs.

52
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:23,520
更多人转向移动支付，国际旅行增加，诈骗模式也发生了变化。
More people shifted to mobile payment, international travel increased, scam pattern changed.

53
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:26,560
现在旧模型的性能下降了。
Now old model performance decline.

54
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,240
这就会产生风险。
This creates risk.

55
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:31,920
如果模型漏掉欺诈行为，银行就会损失金钱。
If model misuse fraud, bank loses money.

56
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,160
如果模型拦截了真实用户，客户就会感到愤怒。
If model block genuine users, customers become angry.

57
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:52,240
MLOps 通过监控欺诈检测的精确率和召回率、检测输入数据的变化、触发重新训练流水线、
测试候选模型以及安全地部署改进版本来解决这个问题。
MLOB solved this by monitoring fraud detection precision and recall, detecting changes in incoming data,
triggering retraining pipelines, testing candidate models, deploying improved version safety.

58
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:57,412
这就是为什么 MLOps 直接影响到收入和客户信任。
This is why MLOPs directly impact revenue and customer trust.

59
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:03,440
现在让我们来看看传统软件与这些模型之间的区别。
Now let's consider traditional software versus the envelopes.

60
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,520
让我们对比一下。
Let's compare them.

61
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:07,120
传统软件。
Traditional software.

62
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,680
开发人员编写明确的规则。
Developers write explicit rules.

63
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:15,920
例如，如果用户的年龄低于这个值，就拒绝申请。
For example, if user age is below it, reject application.

64
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:18,400
流式输入对应流式输出。
Stream input gives stream output.

65
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:23,120
主要关注点是核心质量、功能、性能和安全性。
Main concerns are core quality, works, performance, security.

66
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:29,040
机器学习系统，也就是 ML 系统，是从历史数据中学习的。
Machine learning system ML system learn from historical data.

67
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:38,160
输出取决于数据质量、特征使用、训练方法、超参数、模型权重以及当前的现实世界行为。
Outputs depend on data quality, feature use, training method, hyperparameters, model weight, current real world behavior.

68
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:48,560
所以现在你不仅要管理代码，还要管理数据集、流水线、实验、模型、重训逻辑和监控指标。
So now you must manage not only code but also data sets, pipelines, experiments, models, retraining logic, monitoring metrics.

69
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:54,400
这就是为什么 MLOps 比普通的软件工程更动态、也更复杂。
That is why MLOPS is more dynamic and more complex than the normal software engineering.

70
00:05:55,470 --> 00:05:56,612
容器化。
Containerization.

71
00:05:57,934 --> 00:05:59,556
现在我们来聊聊 Docker。
Now let's talk about Docker.

72
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:03,716
Docker 被用来把你的模型和它所需的一切打包在一起。
Docker is used to package your model with everything it needs.

73
00:06:03,950 --> 00:06:11,556
例如，你的欺诈检测模型需要 Python、Pandas 和 Fast TPM。
For example, your fraud detection model needs Python, Pandas, Fast TPM.

74
00:06:12,078 --> 00:06:15,268
如果服务器没有相同的配置，模型就可能运行失败。
If server does not have the same setup, model may fail.

75
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:18,692
Docker 把所有东西打包进一个容器里。
Docker packs everything together into one container.

76
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:23,556
所以无论是在笔记本、云端还是服务器上运行，它的表现都是一样的。
So whether it runs on laptop, cloud or server, it behaves the same.

77
00:06:24,622 --> 00:06:28,932
因此，Docker 能帮助你的模型在任何地方可靠地运行。
So Docker helps your model run anywhere reliably.

78
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:32,324
让我们再考虑另一个，Kubernetes。
Let's consider another one, Kubernetes.

79
00:06:33,006 --> 00:06:35,620
现在假设一个 Docker 容器不够用了。
Now suppose one Docker container is not enough.

80
00:06:35,982 --> 00:06:39,268
你的银行应用接收到数十万次请求。
Your banking app receives lakhs of requests.

81
00:06:40,366 --> 00:06:42,180
一台服务器可能会过载。
One server may become overloaded.

82
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,036
这就是 Kubernetes 发挥作用的地方。
This is where Kubernetes helps.

83
00:06:44,782 --> 00:06:52,708
Kubernetes 可以运行多个容器，在流量高峰时增加容器，重启故障容器，并自动平衡流量。
Kubernetes can run many containers, increase containers during heavy traffic, restart 12 containers, balance traffic automatically.

84
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:57,680
例如，在发工资期间，交易量会增加。
For example, during salary, transaction volume increases.

85
00:06:57,966 --> 00:07:00,292
Kubernetes 会自动扩展系统。
Kubernetes scales system automatically.

86
00:07:02,446 --> 00:07:03,492
CI/CD 流水线。
CI CD pipeline.

87
00:07:03,854 --> 00:07:05,860
CI/CD 流水线意味着自动化。
CI CD pipeline means automation.

88
00:07:06,254 --> 00:07:08,160
CI 是持续集成。
CI continuous integration.

89
00:07:08,462 --> 00:07:09,956
CD 是持续部署。
C D continuous deployment.

90
00:07:10,446 --> 00:07:14,560
每当开发人员改进代码或模型时，测试就会自动运行。
Whenever developers improve code or model, tests run automatically.

91
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:17,892
系统会检查错误，并安全地部署新版本。
Errors are checked, new versions get deployed safely.

92
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:21,440
例如，新的欺诈模型表现比旧的好。
For example, new fraud model performs better than old one.

93
00:07:21,934 --> 00:07:25,540
CI/CD 流水线可以自动进行测试和部署，无需人工干预。
CI CD pipeline can test it and deploy it without manual work.

94
00:07:25,934 --> 00:07:27,844
这节省了时间并减少了错误。
This saves time and reduces mistakes.

95
00:07:28,622 --> 00:07:31,908
监控方面，我们使用 Prometheus 和 Grafana。
Monitoring We use Prometheus and Grafana.

96
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:35,360
模型上线后，我们必须对其进行监控。
Once model is live, we must monitor it.

97
00:07:35,694 --> 00:07:37,380
比如 API 变慢了吗？
Which a is API slow?

98
00:07:37,742 --> 00:07:38,880
错误率是否在上升？
Are error increasing?

99
00:07:39,118 --> 00:07:40,356
CPU 是否过载了？
Is CPU overloaded?

100
00:07:40,622 --> 00:07:42,560
预测质量是否在下降？
Is prediction quality dropping?

101
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:48,836
Prometheus 会收集响应时间、请求数、CPU 使用率和错误率等指标。
Prometheus and Prometheus collect metrics like response time, request count, CPU usage, error rate.

102
00:07:49,166 --> 00:07:53,604
而 Grafana 则将这些指标以仪表盘、图表、曲线和警报的形式展示出来。
While Grafana shows these metrics as dashboard, charts, graph alerts.

103
00:07:54,190 --> 00:07:57,124
这样团队成员就能直观地了解系统的健康状况。
So team can equally understand systems health.

104
00:07:57,998 --> 00:08:01,636
简单来说，Prometheus 负责收集数据，Grafana 负责数据可视化。
Simple meaning Prometheus collect data, Grafana visualize data.

105
00:08:02,414 --> 00:08:03,844
数据漂移和模型漂移。
Data drift and model drift.

106
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,412
这是非常重要的概念。
Very important concept.

107
00:08:05,838 --> 00:08:08,804
数据漂移是指现实世界中的输入数据发生了变化。
Data drift is real-world input data changes.

108
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:12,996
例如，欺诈模型主要是在卡支付数据上训练的。
For example, fraud model trained mostly on card payments.

109
00:08:13,198 --> 00:08:16,004
现在用户转向了移动钱包和 UPI。
Now user shifted to mobile wallets and UPN.

110
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:17,476
输入模式发生了变化。
Input pattern changed.

111
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:24,068
模型漂移是指即使数据看起来相似，其行为含义也发生了变化。
Model drift, even if data looks similar, behavior meaning changes.

112
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:27,684
例如，昨晚的交易以前被认为是可疑的。
For example, last night transactions were suspicious earlier.

113
00:08:28,014 --> 00:08:30,596
但现在午夜在线购物是正常的。
Now online shopping at midnight is normal.

114
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:33,476
旧模型的逻辑就过时了。
Old model logic becomes outdated.

115
00:08:33,998 --> 00:08:37,220
MLOps 可以检测到这些问题并触发重新训练。
M LOPS detect these problems and triggers retraining.

116
00:08:38,830 --> 00:08:44,080
MLflow 和 TensorFlow 数据验证。
ML flow and TensorFlow data validation.

117
00:08:46,350 --> 00:08:52,452
MLflow，当你训练很多模型时，很难记住哪个模型以及最高的准确率是多少。
ML flow, when you train many models, it becomes hard to remember which model and best accuracy.

118
00:08:53,998 --> 00:08:59,748
MLflow 可以追踪实验、参数、指标和模型版本。
Which settings for ML flow tracks experiments, parameters, metrics, model versions.

119
00:09:00,366 --> 00:09:02,180
TensorFlow 数据验证。
TensorFlow data validation.

120
00:09:02,384 --> 00:09:04,292
这个工具用于检查数据质量。
This tool checks data quality.

121
00:09:05,166 --> 00:09:10,756
例如，如果年龄列突然出现了 500 这样的数值，那就说明出问题了。
For example, if age column suddenly has values like 500, something is wrong.

122
00:09:11,054 --> 00:09:15,492
它有助于检测缺失值、错误的数据类型以及数据分布的变化。
It helps detect missing values, wrong data type, data distribution changes.

123
00:09:15,664 --> 00:09:17,252
在训练之前非常有用。
Very useful before training.

124
00:09:19,086 --> 00:09:24,228
让我们来看看完整的机器学习 MLOps 工作流。
Let's consider complete ML MLOps workflow.

125
00:09:24,846 --> 00:09:26,756
现在让我们看看完整的生命周期。
Now let's see the full life cycle.

126
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:28,932
第一步是数据收集。
The step one is data collection.

127
00:09:29,486 --> 00:09:33,380
从应用程序、交易、数据库和日志中收集数据。
Collect data from apps, transaction, databases, and logs.

128
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:35,684
第二步是数据验证。
Step two is data validation.

129
00:09:36,142 --> 00:09:38,116
检查数据是否干净且正确。
Check if data is clean and correct.

130
00:09:38,638 --> 00:09:46,788
第三步是特征工程，意思是你要为模型创建有用的输入，例如过去 7 天的交易情况。
The third step is feature engineering, means you have to create useful inputs for model, for example, transaction in last 7 days.

131
00:09:47,502 --> 00:09:49,060
第 4 步是模型训练。
Step 4 model training.

132
00:09:49,710 --> 00:09:56,132
训练像 Random Forest、XGBoost 和神经网络之类的算法。
Train algorithm like random forest, XGBoost, neural networks.

133
00:09:56,782 --> 00:09:58,308
第 5 步是评估。
Step 5 is evaluation.

134
00:09:58,734 --> 00:10:03,364
检查各项指标，如准确率、精确率、召回率和 F1 分数。
Check metrics, accuracy, precision, recall, F1 score.

135
00:10:03,854 --> 00:10:05,744
第 6 步是模型注册。
Step 6 is register model.

136
00:10:06,222 --> 00:10:07,524
保存通过审核的版本。
Save approved version.

137
00:10:08,302 --> 00:10:12,580
第 7 步是使用 Docker 进行容器化打包。
Step 7 containerize package using Docker.

138
00:10:13,326 --> 00:10:14,564
第 8 步是部署。
Step 8 deploy.

139
00:10:14,990 --> 00:10:16,804
部署到云端或 Kubernetes 上。
Deploy on cloud or Kubernetes.

140
00:10:17,518 --> 00:10:19,268
第 9 步是监控。
Step 9 is monitor it.

141
00:10:19,598 --> 00:10:21,444
追踪速度、故障和漂移。
Track speed failure drift.

142
00:10:22,190 --> 00:10:24,388
第 10 步是重新训练。
And step 10 is retrain.

143
00:10:24,878 --> 00:10:27,172
使用最新的测试数据并重复这个循环。
Use led test data and repeat cycle.

144
00:10:27,344 --> 00:10:28,996
这就变成了一个持续的循环。
This becomes a continuous loop.

145
00:10:29,806 --> 00:10:31,332
那么谁应该学习 MLOps？
So who should learn MLOPs?

146
00:10:31,758 --> 00:10:39,264
数据科学家需要部署模型而不仅仅是停留在笔记本上，机器学习工程师需要构建生产环境。
Data scientists to deploy models instead of stopping at notebooks, ML engineers to build production.

147
00:10:39,438 --> 00:10:49,124
AI 系统、DevOps 工程师负责管理基础设施和流水线，
云工程师负责在 AWS、Azure 上运行可扩展的系统。
AI systems, DevOps engineers to manage infrastructure and pipelines, cloud engineers to run scalable systems on AWS, Azure.

148
00:10:49,344 --> 00:10:54,852
还有 GCP，工程经理负责管理团队、时间线和系统可靠性。
GCP, engineering managers to manage teams, timelines, and system reliability.

149
00:10:55,502 --> 00:10:57,860
为什么 MLOPS 是一项有价值的职业技能？
Why MLOPS is a valuable career skill?

150
00:10:58,384 --> 00:11:00,772
很多人知道如何训练模型。
Many people know how to train models.

151
00:11:01,198 --> 00:11:04,676
但很少有人知道如何在生产环境中运行它们。
Few people know how to run them in production.

152
00:11:05,166 --> 00:11:08,580
这就是为什么 MLOps 角色非常有价值的原因。
That is why MLOPs roles are highly valuable.

153
00:11:09,134 --> 00:11:12,996
公司需要能利用人工智能创造商业价值的人。
Company needs people who can create business value using AI.

154
00:11:14,894 --> 00:11:17,824
所以记住，机器学习是创造智能。
So remember this machine learning creates intelligence.

155
00:11:18,126 --> 00:11:21,700
而 MLOps 是在现实世界中交付这些智能。
MLOPS delivers intelligence in the real world.

156
00:11:22,126 --> 00:11:27,076
还有一个重要的事实是，模型训练完成并不代表成功。
And one more powerful truth is a model is not successful when it is trained.

157
00:11:27,264 --> 00:11:30,116
只有当它解决了真实的业务问题时，它才是成功的。
It is successful when it solves real business problem.

158
00:11:30,798 --> 00:11:37,476
